5G-LENA (NR v3.3), model/nr-mac-scheduler-ns3.cc: the assertion at the end of DoSchedUlSrInfoReq compares the
merged list of UEs that asked for an uplink grant with the list just received. The list just received can name the
same UE twice (two scheduling requests of one UE delivered together, which happens when uplink slots are sparse and
many UEs have data); the merge above the assertion handles that correctly, the assertion does not, and a build with
assertions enabled aborts. The assertion is made to compare with the number of DISTINCT UEs. No behaviour changes.

Applied by simulation/run_sweep.py (once; `git -C ns-3-dev/contrib/nr apply`).

--- a/model/nr-mac-scheduler-ns3.cc
+++ b/model/nr-mac-scheduler-ns3.cc
@@ -2581,7 +2581,10 @@ NrMacSchedulerNs3::DoSchedUlSrInfoReq(
             m_srList.push_back(ue);
         }
     }
-    NS_ASSERT(m_srList.size() >= params.m_srList.size());
+    // Kyber-6G: the received list may name one UE twice; compare with the number of distinct UEs
+    NS_ASSERT(m_srList.size() >=
+              std::unordered_set<uint16_t>(params.m_srList.begin(), params.m_srList.end())
+                  .size());
 }

